ml2165-rust (1.2.0-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Close the QPDL stream with the closing UEL when a job is cancelled:
    the filter now handles SIGTERM, stops at the next band boundary and
    exits 0, instead of being killed mid-band and leaving the printer in
    QPDL mode.
  * Drop the per-job limits (1000 pages, 8 GiB of raster, 10000 sheets);
    long documents now print. Copies are still capped at 999 per page, and
    CUPS' own job-page-limit is the place for quotas.
  * Remove the unreachable manual-duplex path. The PPD never offered duplex,
    so jobs were and remain single-sided (DUPLEX=OFF).
  * Non-ASCII characters in the PJL job and user names are now dropped
    instead of folded to ASCII; the ML-2165 does not display either field.
  * The data sent to the printer is otherwise unchanged for every supported
    paper size, resolution, paper type and tray.
  * Build with rustc 1.97.1 or newer, and produce the package with
    packaging/build-deb.sh (dpkg-deb) instead of assembling it by hand.
    Packages are reproducible: the same commit gives byte-identical .debs.
  * Also build for arm64, cross-compiled on amd64. The test suite passes
    under qemu-user and the data sent to the printer is byte-identical to
    the amd64 build.

 -- CUPS Raster Filter Developer <caganergun@tutanota.com>  Sun, 08 Nov 2026 20:28:48 +0300

ml2165-rust (1.1.0-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Narrow the driver to the USB-attached Samsung ML-2165: the ML-2160,
    ML-2165W and ML-2168 product entries are gone from the PPD, and the
    documentation no longer describes network or Wi-Fi setups.
  * Rename the source and binary package from samsung-ml2160-rust; the PPD
    ships as samsung-ml2165.ppd under /usr/share/ppd/ml2165-rust/.
    Existing queues keep working until they are re-registered, because the
    filter binary name (rastertospl-rust) is unchanged.
  * Take the *ImageableArea margins from upstream SpliX ml2165.ppd: 12.5 pt
    on every edge instead of 12 pt.
  * Build the filter against glibc instead of statically against musl, and
    declare the resulting runtime dependencies (libc6, libgcc-s1). Supported
    platforms are Debian 13 (trixie) and Debian 14.

 -- CUPS Raster Filter Developer <caganergun@tutanota.com>  Sat, 12 Sep 2026 14:30:00 +0300

